part.text:
Fixed. The bug: after `removeSheetByIndex(0)` removes the last sheet, `activeSheetIndex` becomes -1, and `addSheet()` with an explicit index never restored it — so later style application called `setActiveSheetIndex(-1)` and threw.

The fix in `src/PhpSpreadsheet/Spreadsheet.php:823` — when inserting a sheet at an explicit index while the active index is negative, set the active index to the inserted sheet's actual position:

```php
if ($this->activeSheetIndex >= $sheetIndex) {
    ++$this->activeSheetIndex;
} elseif ($this->activeSheetIndex < 0) {
    $this->activeSheetIndex = max(0, $this->getIndex($worksheet));
}
```

Validated: the issue's repro script now works, `Issue4112Test` (all 5 data sets, including negative and out-of-range indices) passes, and the full suite shows no regressions beyond pre-existing environment failures (GD images/fonts/file permissions, confirmed identical on the unmodified baseline).
